# Local exploratory A_core versus C1

The immutable protocol and SHA-256 seal precede real fitting. Original certified
harness, cohort, preflight and snapshots remain untouched. No network or DB access.

Runtime: `work/avm-01-20261008/.venv-repro/Scripts/python.exe`, Python 3.13.4.
Use `-B` on each invocation. All commands below refer to this directory's scripts.

1. `pilot.py prepare` (once only; already prepared).
2. `test_pilot.py` (synthetic negative controls and real lineage, without real fits).
3. `pilot.py run G3 20261009 principal`.
4. Repeat in a fresh process: `pilot.py run G3 20261009 reproduction`.
5. Fixed sensitivities: `run G3 20261010 G3-20261010`,
   `run G3 20261011 G3-20261011`, and `run G1 SEED G1-SEED` for each of
   20261009, 20261010 and 20261011. G2 is verified identical-input reuse of G1.
6. `pilot.py analyze`; `test_pilot.py`; `pilot.py verify`; `pilot.py finalize`.

Scenario files refuse overwrite. Independent scenarios may run in separate
processes; each has process-local label custody and distinct output files.
Further exact reproduction may use a new tag with the same registered group/seed.

`own_valid` and `paired_common` metrics answer different questions. All coverage
denominators use the full eligible view. Error percentages are in percentage
points; APE threshold fractions are 0–1. Bootstrap intervals condition on fixed
OOF predictions and do not represent independent training repetitions.

`C1` includes publication source, not coordinates. No source is justified yet for
manual valuations. UF-native offers are not transaction prices; identity and area
precision remain limited. This is not production readiness or a final holdout.

Prices/predictions stay within this private NTFS-protected experimental folder.
No external publishing, original artifact edits or productive changes permitted.
